module newtype.pos_1

// A NEWTYPE and its constructor, and the effect is visible: prints 7, byte for
// byte with the oracle.
//
// `type Row int` is a DISTINCT type over the representation `int` -- the oracle
// enforces the distinction (a `Row` into an `int` parameter is E7301, measured
// by the integrator 2026-08-21). At runtime it IS the representation, zero cost:
// the oracle writes `typedef nova_int Nova_Row;` and then a plain `nova_int`
// local, and novac emits the argument with no wrapper at all.
//
// novac refused the DECLARATION until 2026-08-21 with "this is not a form of the
// language" -- about a form the language has -- because `@type_decl` read only
// three tails (generics, `enum`/pipes, a brace body) and let any other fall into
// the top-level junk bucket. And the CONSTRUCTOR iced: `Row(7)` reached the
// lattice, which answered "internal compiler error" at a legal program.
//
// This form is what the registry indices of novac itself are waiting for (plan
// 274 section 9.1g): a `row` and a `ty_id` are different spaces of the same
// `int` today, and they can only be told apart by a type once novac reads the
// type that tells them apart.
type Row int

fn main() {
    ro r = Row(7)
    println(r)
}
